Fixes #1855

The `CSSStyleDeclaration` class was missing the `Symbol.iterator` implementation, which prevented users from iterating over style properties using `for...of` loops, the spread operator, or `Array.from()`.

## Changes

- Added `[Symbol.iterator]()` generator method to `CSSStyleDeclaration` class
- Added tests for iteration functionality

## Before

```javascript
const myElement = document.createElement('div');
myElement.setAttribute('style', 'background:red');

for (const key of myElement.style) {
  console.log(key);
}
// TypeError: myElement.style is not iterable
```

## After

```javascript
const myElement = document.createElement('div');
myElement.setAttribute('style', 'background:red');

for (const key of myElement.style) {
  console.log(key);
}
// Outputs: background-image, background-position-x, background-position-y, etc.

// Also works with spread operator
console.log([...myElement.style]);

// And Array.from()
console.log(Array.from(myElement.style));
```

### Packages impacted by this PR

- `@typespec/ts-http-runtime`

### Issues associated with this PR

Related to Azure Blob Storage batch operations and other services returning `multipart/mixed` responses.

### Describe the problem that is addressed by this PR

The runtime supports sending multipart requests but lacks parsing for multipart responses. Services like Azure Blob Storage `submitBatch` return `multipart/mixed` responses that were unparseable, forcing consumers to handle raw string bodies.

### What are the possible designs available to address the problem? If there are more than one possible design, why was the one in this PR chosen?

**Design**: Automatic parsing in `getResponseBody()` when `Content-Type: multipart/*` is detected, returning structured `MultipartResponseBody` with typed parts.

**Alternative**: Manual parsing API requiring consumers to explicitly call parsing functions. Rejected - violates existing pattern where response bodies are automatically parsed (JSON, text).

### Are there test cases added in this PR? _(If not, why?)_

Yes. 30+ test cases covering:
- Multiple parts with various headers
- CRLF/LF line ending variations  
- Empty parts and edge cases
- Azure Blob Storage batch response format
- Integration with `sendRequest()`

### Provide a list of related PRs _(if any)_

None

### Command used to generate this PR:**_(Applicable only to SDK release request PRs)_

N/A

### Checklists
- [x] Added impacted package name to the issue description
- [ ] Does this PR needs any fixes in the SDK Generator?** _(If so, create an Issue in the [Autorest/typescript](https://github.com/Azure/autorest.typescript) repository and link it here)_
- [ ] Added a changelog (if necessary)

---

## Implementation

**New module**: `src/client/multipartResponse.ts`
- `parseMultipartResponse(body, boundary)` - RFC 2046 compliant parser
- `isMultipartContentType(contentType)` - Content-Type detector
- `getBoundaryFromContentType(contentType)` - Boundary extractor with quote handling

**Modified**: `src/client/sendRequest.ts`
```typescript
function getResponseBody(response: PipelineResponse) {
  const contentType = response.headers.get("content-type") ?? "";

  // New: Automatic multipart parsing
  if (isMultipartContentType(contentType)) {
    const boundary = getBoundaryFromContentType(contentType);
    if (boundary && response.bodyAsText) {
      return parseMultipartResponse(response.bodyAsText, boundary);
    }
  }
  // ... existing JSON/text handling
}
```

**Modified**: `src/client/common.ts`
- Extended `FullOperationResponse.parsedBody` type to include `MultipartResponseBody`

**Exports**: Types and functions added to public API via `src/index.ts`

## Usage

```typescript
const response = await client.path("/batch").post({ body: batchRequest });

// Response body now automatically parsed for multipart/mixed
if (response.body && 'parts' in response.body) {
  for (const part of response.body.parts) {
    console.log(part.headers["Content-Type"]);
    console.log(new TextDecoder().decode(part.body));
  }
}
```

